{"name":"Tamed Beast","hex":"#9c2626","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tamed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["domesticated; made tame"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of tame"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tamed"},{"term":"beast","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any four-footed land mammal.","All non-human animals seen as a group."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To impose arduous exercise upon, either as training or as punishment.","To bully or harass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beast"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tame animal","blocks":[{"text":"A tame animal is an animal that is relatively tolerant of human presence. Tameness may arise naturally or due to the deliberate, human-directed process of training an animal against its initially wild or natural instincts to avoid or attack humans. The tameability of an animal is the level of ease it takes humans to train the animal, and varies among individual animals, breeds, or species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Feeding_a_squirrel_in_Kensington_Park_%2810144548845%29.jpg/330px-Feeding_a_squirrel_in_Kensington_Park_%2810144548845%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tame_animal","wikidata":"Q247285"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Deer_roaming_in_Nara_city._2010.jpg/500px-Deer_roaming_in_Nara_city._2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Deer_roaming_in_Nara_city._2010.jpg/500px-Deer_roaming_in_Nara_city._2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tame deer in Nara","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeer_roaming_in_Nara_city._2010.jpg"}],"sounds":{"beast":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/En-us-beast.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a2/En-us-beast.ogg/En-us-beast.ogg.mp3"}]}}}